      "message": "I think we do require the `.` preceding the `*` in regex since the \"*\" is simply a quantifier token/repetition operator that analyzes for the expression immediately preceding it, where in this case I believe we want to capture any characters (`.`) before the string \"Precompile\". \nhttps://web.mit.edu/gnu/doc/html/regex_toc.html#SEC12\n\nThe intent here was to capture any file at this path with `Precompile` in its name (and not just those with `Precompile` as the **starting** word of a class name) for some level of future-proofing.\n\nLMK if I am misunderstanding!",
